I finally made it. I actually never made it to Gehemnon before.
I started with a protection run to the mines. I eventually had to kill
some gas spores and reached lvl2, which simplified matters. I got to
minetown without major problemes.

Trouble #1: my pet fell down through some trapdoor. I still had not
enough protection- since I had a magic whistle I planned on getting my
AC to 1 with stolen money from the shops. I had a magic whistle which
recovered my pet once I had run through all kinds of monsters to the
downstairs. I got my pet back to gnometown just to fall through the
next trapdoor... ouch. 2 levels down. With heavy
Elbereth/running/praying I made it up again. I identified a ruby, sold
it, had my pet steal it back and sold ist again. So I got my intrinsic
AC of 1.
I bought a magic lamp from Itzchak and got me a SDSM and got my
luckstone from the Mines.
Trouble #2: Since I found a BoH in the mines I skipped Sokoban and did
some altar-lurking on dl 10. It got me some good books and magicbane
but eventually I fucked it up and prayed when I should not have. ouch.
I lost 9 protection and Anhur was angry. I decided I would have to fix
Anhur's anger before descending deeper, so I would be able to pray at
emergencies. So I wrote a nice cursed scoll of genocide and, well,
reverse genocided master mind flayers after engraving Elbereth all over
the place. None left me a corpse though, so I descended further. Later
I spent an additional magic-lamp-wish on frostbrand.

On dlvl 24 I found a neutral temple, which I converted and used for
some additional altar lurking. I got to lvl 20 with some wraith-lurking
on a gravyard somewhere before and dlv 24 produced worthwhile
sacrafices. The altarlurking ended whith my crowning. I killed medusa
(with a zap of finger of death!) and genocided arch-liches and did my
quest. Then I did the castle- rather simple, blast the door, put on
levitation and kill everything whith fireball and cone of cold and +7
frostbrand. Then I descended into Gehennom.
Somewhere in Gehennom I tested out some wands and found out I had a
wand of wishing. cool. As I heard now one is guaranteed in the castle,
so I should have used it right away. I decided to do a stash relocate
from dlv 12 to the castle then and ended wishing of a helm of
brilliance and a book of polymorph and sparing 3 whishes for
emergencies (never used them). Happy times of polypiling followed, as
well as writing of ?oCharge and +oIdentify.
Next I got the candelabrum and marked the VS. The demons were no
problems, Juiblex got his belly ripped and the peaceful Asmodeus got
stoned. I payed off Beelzebub and killed Orcus and Yeenoghu after the
tiresome way back from Orcus room to the upstairs. (every 2 or 3 turns
one of the two showed up, hit me once, got a magic missle and was away)
Last preparation for the ascension run included digging a way for the
run, some nurse-dancing, enchanting my stuff to max and polypiling for
"oLS (never needed one) and =oP. I got my intrinsic AC to 0 eating
charged-up =oPs. I actually tried out to mass-produce magic markers
with reverse genociding white unicorns and polypiling the horns. It did
not work and I probably wasted a real bunch of marker charges on
trying.

Then I started the run. Rodney died easily to Finger of Death as well
as molochs high priest. I got the amulett and started runnung up.
Rodney proved really harmless- he died with one FoD and magicbane
catched most curses. In the castle I took my time to sort my stash a
last time, get some potions and holy water and polypile my excess
wands. I finally continued my run two dead Rodneys later with a
well-chosen collection of wands. Reaching dlvl 1 was easy, as well as
Earth. I located the portals with 4 ?oGd. On Air I got a final gift
from Ptah: He sent an Archon with Sunsword to kill me. Great, I thought
and charmed him and named him "gift_of_ptah".
On the Astral Plane I walked quite... chaotic. Firstly I killed
pestilence and saw some priest of Ptah, so I thought "probably the
wrong one". Next Death. I teleported Angels, priests, etc away or
zapped them with my /oD. Death himself I killed with magic missles on
entereing the temple (wrong one). On leaving the temple I didn't bother
anymore but ran. Next I retried the temple I had dismissed at first.
Pestilence again. Wrong one again. On my run to the last temple I
encountered Peltilence and Famine (2x) but they were easily disposed
with a zap of Death.

